{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0140547","isObsolete":false,"name":"acquisition of seed longevity","definition":{"text":"The acquisition of seed longevity is the ordered series of events during seed development, that prevent embryo deterioration and ROS damage and thus contribute to seed viability over time or in response to adverse environmental conditions. These events include protective (e.g. production of glassy cytoplasm ) and repair (e.g. oxidative stress responses) processes.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"26637538"}]},"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-03-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-02-24","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0022414 (reproductive process)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-24","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0032501 (multicellular organismal process)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-24","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009791 (post-embryonic development)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-14","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009791 (post-embryonic development)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-14","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"acquisition of seed longevity"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-14","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0022414 (reproductive process)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-14","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0048316 (seed development)"},{"timestamp":"2020-11-14","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The acquisition of seed longevity is the ordered series of events during seed development, that prevent embryo deterioration and ROS damage and thus contribute to seed viability over time or in response to adverse environmental conditions. These events include protective (e.g. production of glassy cytoplasm ) and repair (e.g. oxidative stress responses) processes."}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0140547","ancestorName":"acquisition of seed longevity","rela